{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"$\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]$ is the *second derivative* of $5\\ln(x^5)$. In other words, it's the derivative of $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]$, which is the derivative of $5\\ln(x^5)$.\n\nTherefore, in order to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]$, we need to differentiate $5\\ln(x^5)$ twice.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"Let's start by finding $\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]$:\n\n$\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]=\\dfrac{25}{x}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\ln(x^5)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\left(\\dfrac{1}{x^5}\\right)\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[x^5\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{5}{x^5}\\cdot5x^4\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{25}{x}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"Now we can differentiate $\\dfrac{25}{x}$ to find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]$:\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{25}{x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{25}{x^2}\n\\end{align}$\n\n[[☃ explanation 1]]","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{"explanation 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"explanation":"$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{25}{x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=25\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[\\dfrac{1}{x}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=25\\cdot\\dfrac{d}{dx}\\left[x^{-1}\\right]\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=25\\cdot(-x^{-2})\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-25x^{-2}\n\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=-\\dfrac{25}{x^2}\n\\end{align}$","hidePrompt":"Got it, thanks!","showPrompt":"Show entire calculation.","static":false,"widgets":{}},"static":false,"type":"explanation","version":{"major":0,"minor":0}}}},{"content":"In conclusion, $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]=-\\dfrac{25}{x^2}$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Find $\\dfrac{d^2}{dx^2}\\left[5\\ln(x^5)\\right]$.**\n\n[[☃ expression 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"expression 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"answerForms":[{"considered":"correct","form":false,"key":0,"simplify":false,"value":"-\\frac{25}{x^2}"}],"buttonSets":["basic","prealgebra"],"functions":["f","g","h"],"times":false},"static":false,"type":"expression","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
